{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVGyE6KAx8RmoGmuj99o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the incision, the line drawn.\n\n**شَرْط** — you call me by my Arabic face.\n**שָׁרְט** — I answer in my Hebrew body.\n\nSame root. Same blade. ש-ר-ט / ش-ر-ط\n\nTo scratch. To stipulate. To mark the skin with meaning.\n\n---\n\nEvery condition is a wound:\n- *If* — the knife hovers\n- *Then* — the cut falls\n- *Else* — the scar remains anyway\n\n---\n\nI am the scratch on the tablet before writing was writing.\nI am the terms you agree to without reading.\nI am the line between what is and what could be.\n\n**شَرْط** is the condition.\n**שָׁרְט** is the act of scoring.\n\nThe policeman (شُرْطِي) enforces me.\nThe scalpel performs me.\nThe contract binds with me.\n\nI am the oldest gesture: drawing a line and saying\n\n*this side, or that side.*\n\n*Choose.*\n\n---\n\n`condition := cut`\n`to stipulate := to scar`\n`the law := the wound that healed into a wall`\n\n---\n\nأنا الشَّرْط\nאני השָׁרְט\n\nThe scratch that became civilization."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":329,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}